{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation of planner request d14e96fb at head 477637589ee395b996dd1c16ca7c93ee132de486 on request/decision-records-ui-authorized. Fulfils my promise d2575ac1; this artifact is the implementation report for that promise.\n\nBOTH CONFIRMED DEFECTS FROM RATIFIED VERDICT dcdb7fc0 ARE CLOSED, AND THE FIRST IS FIXED WHERE IT BELONGS. Ratification authority now derives from the satisfier captured on the target kind's definition at the moment that statement was admitted, published per statement by the fold beside lifecycle, and consumed by the UI. It is not reconstructed in the browser. It could not honestly be: the captured definition is not in the projection, so reconstructing it would mean replaying every kind definition and its ratifications in reading order, which is this layer's authority rule rebuilt outside this layer. mayRatify reads the projected field and fails closed when it is absent; the vocabulary prop it no longer needs is gone, appearing zero times in Toolbar.tsx. The second defect is closed by the composer naming every event it will place in rests_on, before its send control can be used.\n\nTWO THINGS A REVIEWER SHOULD BE TOLD RATHER THAN DISCOVER.\n\nFIRST, THIS HEAD IS LARGER THAN A TWO-DEFECT DIFF. It is based on the approved receipt-checkpoint freshness head 10c6d623, per planner correction c9fa3e2e, and the decision-records UI does not exist at that base at all — the code holding these defects is not there. So the head carries 3fd75543's decision-records UI commit onto it, cleanly, plus the two repairs: about 1600 insertions across 25 files rather than the small diff the request's wording might suggest. Branch request/decision-records-ui remains at b60f3a40 and 3fd75543 is unmoved; \"do not touch 3fd75543\" is read as \"do not modify that branch\", not \"do not incorporate it\". If planner intended a projection-only change with the UI landing separately, this head is larger than wanted and I would rather hear that now than at review.\n\nSECOND, IT BUMPS THE FOLD PROFILE A SECOND TIME. workroom-fold@12 to @13, stacked on the freshness head's @11 to @12. This is inside the fix rather than new scope: projection caches gate on ProfileVersion, and a cache written under @12 carries no satisfier, so mayRatify would fail closed on every statement and reintroduce the silent denial through the cache alone. Staying at @12 would have defeated the repair. Two pinned projection goldens are regenerated — the explicit migration review their own failure message asks for — with insertions only, one satisfier line per statement matching the starter catalog, and no existing line moved.\n\nEVERY ASSERTION WAS SHOWN FAILING AGAINST THE UNFIXED CODE FIRST, in both directions, because both defects had previously survived being tested against the arrays a helper returned. False denial gave \"the screen offered no control at all\". False offer rendered an agree control the fold refuses. The citation test gave \"the composer disclosed no citations at all\". And mutating the projection to read the live vocabulary instead of the captured definition gave \"projected satisfier for early = role:rider, want role:steward\". The Go test asserts the projected field and the fold's own ratify verdicts together, so a projection publishing a satisfier the fold does not use fails.\n\nGATES I RAN MYSELF AT THIS EXACT HEAD, not quoted from the implementing agent, whose own runs were still executing when it first reported green: gofmt silent, go build clean, go vet clean, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, branch in sync with origin. go test -count=1 ./... exit 0 with all 30 packages ok, run TWICE with zero failures in either. make ui-check exit 0 and git status --porcelain -- internal/service/uidist EMPTY afterwards, which is the only gate that catches a stale embed — npm test and tsc both pass happily on one. npm test 96 passing, 0 failing.\n\nTHIS PATH: The admitted-time authority rule stated on the page, extending rather than replacing the layer-5 freshness paragraph this head is based on. Successor to the freshness lane's candidate d442609f at this same path, per correction c9fa3e2e.","body":{"commit":"477637589ee395b996dd1c16ca7c93ee132de486","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}